(a) This article shall not apply to:
(1) So-called "grandfathered" projects, that is, any portion of a property included within the limits of a valid land disturbance permit issued prior to the effective date of the ordinance from which this article is derived, provided that all time constraints relating to the permit issued shall be observed. In no event shall any grandfathered project be extended for a time period greater than 12 months from the date of enactment of the ordinance from which this article is derived;
(2) Removal of any dead, diseased, structurally unsound or infested tree trees which constitute a danger to human life or property as determined by the county extension service, the state forestry commission, a certified arborist, a registered forester or the town manager;
(3) Removal of trees, other than specimen trees, from an owner-occupied, single-family platted lot. Removal shall be limited to removal of no more than five trees per acre that are less than 24 inches in diameter within a single calendar year;
(4) All licensed plant or tree nurseries and farms shall be exempt from the terms and provisions of this article only in relation to those trees which are planted and being grown for sale or intended sale to the general public in the ordinary course of business;
(5) Removal of trees from agricultural or horticultural properties such as farms, nurseries or orchards;
(6) Necessary removal of trees by a utility company within dedicated utility easements;
(7) Removal of trees on public rights-of-way conducted by, on behalf of, or for any activity to be dedicated to a federal, state, county, municipal or other government agency in pursuit of its lawful activities or functions in the construction or improvement of public rights-of-way, including public buildings, streets, drainage systems, recreational facilities and utilities;
(8) Removal of trees, other than specimen trees, from detention ponds and drainage easements; and
(9) Activities which require issuance of a building permit, but do not require or authorize land disturbance.
(b) None of the above exemptions shall be interpreted to include tree removal or timber harvesting incidental to the development of the land. Notwithstanding the foregoing, all reasonable efforts shall be made to save specimen trees.
(Ord. No. 423, § 1(exhibit A, § 1-021), 5-1-2002)
